# -Task A: Create a private repository with a README
 
One-page English guide
 
Prerequisites
 
1. A GitHub account and you are signed in.

2. A desktop web browser.

3. An available repository name.
 
Steps
 
1. On the GitHub homepage, click the + icon in the top-right corner and select New repository.

2. Type your repository name in the box.

3. Select Private to set this repository as private.

4. Tick the checkbox Add a README file.

5. Click the green button Create repository.
